        "anchor": "our-difference",
        "eyebrow": "Our difference",
        "heading": "What we do that the shelf next to us does not",
        "heading_size": "h1",
        "body": "<p>Three specific differences, all of which you can check rather than take on trust.</p><p><strong>We publish doses.</strong> Our niacinamide sits at 2 to 4 percent, not the 10 percent some brands advertise, because above 5 the returns flatten and the flushing risk rises. That is a number we lose comparisons on, printed anyway.</p><p><strong>We formulate for the room the product ends up in.</strong> Ethyl ascorbic acid instead of L-ascorbic acid. Lighter textures than a European equivalent, because a cream that feels right in a Delhi January feels like a film in a Mumbai July.</p><p><strong>We publish what we have not solved.</strong> Hard water strips barriers during the wash and no leave-on product fixes that. We can offer a cleanser that does not add to the problem and a moisturizer that repairs afterwards. We cannot offer a solution, so we do not claim one.</p>",
